  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>Your teacher will give you a <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/65ade6cf04697521f26b3f3f779957e058748fdf">set of cards</link> that each contain a number. Decide whether each number is a possible input for the functions described here. Sort the cards into two groups: possible inputs and impossible inputs. Record your sorting decisions.</para>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>The area of a square, in square centimeters, is a function of its side length, \(s\), in centimeters. The equation \(A(s) =s^2\) defines this function. 
        
     </para>
      <para>Possible inputs:</para>
      </problem><solution>
    
    
  
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
    
    <para>Possible inputs: \(9\), \(\frac35\), \(15\), \(0\), \(0.8\), \(4\), \(\frac{25}4\), \(0.001\), \(6.8\), \(72\)</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Impossible inputs:</para>
      </problem><solution>
    
    
  
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
    
    <para>Impossible inputs: –3, –18</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>A tennis camp charges $40 per student for a full-day camp. The camp only runs if at least 5 students sign up, and it limits the enrollment to 16 campers a day. The amount of revenue, in dollars, that the tennis camp collects is a function of the number of students who enroll.
        The equation \(R(n)=40n\) defines this function. 
        
     </para>
      <para>Possible inputs:</para>
      </problem><solution>
    
    
  
