    <para>The relationship between temperature in Celsius and the temperature in Kelvin can be represented by a function \(k\). The equation \(k(c)=c+273.15\) defines this function, where \(c\) is the temperature in Celsius and \(k(c)\) is the temperature in Kelvin. 
        
     </para>
